-- title:
--   Bottom-layer admissible constants and level field, q=3
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ denotes `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`, $q$ is a prime subject to the hypothesis `hq3` that $q = 3$, and $M'$ is a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$ (`hqM'`). Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $q$ in the sense of `LiesOverPrime`, i.e. $q$ is a nonunit of $A$ (`hA`).
--
--   Reduction data. $W$ is a finite set of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'`, the subfield of Laurent series over the residue field of $A$ generated by `jqModC` and `jqNModC … M'`, over that residue field; `hW` asserts that $W$ consists of exactly the members of `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`, that is, of the places $w$ that are rational, satisfy `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and for which `w.evalAt (jGeomGen …)` lies in `ssJSet q …`. The hypothesis `hle` is the inclusion `modularFunctionFieldBar M' ≤ fieldBar q M'` of the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-base change of the full level-$M'$ modular function field into the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-base change of the function field of $X_H$ at level $q^2M'$ with $H$ the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q)^\times$. Next, $R₀$ is a `ConstantReduction` datum for $A$ on `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` with values in `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'`: a valuation subring $R₀.\mathrm{integers}$, a surjective residue homomorphism onto the target field with kernel the maximal ideal, a map on places preserving degrees, and the compatibilities of membership, of residues of constants from $A$, of scaling, and of divisor pushforward recorded in that structure. The hypothesis `hR₀` says that for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that image lies in $R₀.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R₀$-residue, read as a Laurent series over `ResidueField A`, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$. Finally $\pi \in \overline{\mathbb Q}$ satisfies $\pi^{q^2-1} = q$ (`hπ`) and lies in $A$ (`hπP`), and $\zeta$ is an element of `Idx q`, i.e. a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$.
--
--   Igusa rings. $\mathrm{OIg}$ assigns a valuation subring of `fieldBar q M'` to each point of [`CuspidalType.ProjLine q`](def/CuspidalType_IsCuspidalOfType.html#L21), the projective line over $\mathbb Z/q$. Four hypotheses constrain it: `hIg_inf` characterises the ring at `lineInfty q` (the point $[1:0]$) as consisting of those $f$ for which there are Laurent series $x, y$ over $A$ with the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ nonzero and $f$ times the image of $y$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-coefficients equal to the image of $x$; `hIg` provides, for each point $\ell$, some $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with `redQ q γ • lineInfty q = ℓ` and $\mathrm{OIg}(\ell)$ the pullback of $\mathrm{OIg}(\infty)$ along `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ`; `hIg_inj` asserts injectivity of $\mathrm{OIg}$; and `hIg_perm` asserts that for every $\zeta'$ in `Idx q` and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ the pullbacks along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` permute the family $\mathrm{OIg}$, through some permutation of [`CuspidalType.ProjLine q`](def/CuspidalType_IsCuspidalOfType.html#L21).
--
--   Supersingular rings. $\mathrm{OSS}$ assigns a valuation subring of `fieldBar q M'` to each $s \in W$. Four hypotheses constrain it. `hSS_A` says that for each $s$ and each $x \in \overline{\mathbb Q}$ the constant $x$ lies in $\mathrm{OSS}(s)$ if and only if $x \in A$. `hSS_over` says: for $s \in W$ and $f$ in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` lying in $R₀.\mathrm{integers}$, if $f$ has nonnegative order at every place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at which the element $\hat\jmath$ determined by `coeffEmb (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) jq` has nonnegative order, and if the $R₀$-residue of $f$ lies in the valuation subring of $s$, then the image of $f$ in `fieldBar q M'` under `hle` lies in $\mathrm{OSS}(s)$, and moreover for every $a \in A$ whose residue equals `s.evalAt` of that $R₀$-residue, the difference between the image of $f$ and the constant $a$ lies in $\mathrm{OSS}(s)$ and in the maximal ideal of $\mathrm{OSS}(s)$. `hSS_fix` says each $\mathrm{OSS}(s)$ is carried to itself by pullback along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` for all $\zeta'$ and all $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$. `hSS_tr` provides, for each $s$, an element $t \in \mathrm{OSS}(s)$ such that for every $a \in A$ the difference $t - a$ lies in $\mathrm{OSS}(s)$ and is a unit there.
--
--   Descent base. $K₀$ is a subfield of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ algebraic over it and $\pi \in K₀$ (`hπK₀`). $A₀$ is a henselian discrete valuation domain equipped with an injective local ring homomorphism $\iota : A₀ \to A$ (`hι`) whose image, viewed inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, is exactly $A \cap K₀$ (`hιK₀`), such that the composite of $\iota$ with the residue map of $A$ is surjective (`hres`), and with an element $\varpi_0$ generating the maximal ideal of $A₀$ (`hϖ₀`) whose image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is $\pi$ (`hϖ₀π`). $F₀$ is a subfield of `fieldBar q M'` characterised by `hF₀`: an element belongs to $F₀$ precisely when all its Laurent coefficients lie in $K₀$; by `hjF₀` it contains the image of $\hat\jmath$ under `hle`; and $F₀$ carries an $A₀$-algebra structure whose structure map is, by `hj₀`, the map sending $a$ to the constant $\iota(a)$ of `fieldBar q M'`.
--
--   Conclusion. Under these hypotheses there exist an intermediate field $k₀$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$, an element $\pi_0$ of $k₀$ whose image lies in $A$, such that all of the following hold. (i) The underlying set of $k₀$ equals that of $K₀$, and (ii) $\pi_0 = \pi$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$. Writing $A \cap k₀$ for `A.comap (algebraMap ↥k₀ (AlgebraicClosure ℚ))`: (iii) $A \cap k₀$ is a discrete valuation ring; (iv) its maximal ideal is generated by $\pi_0$; (v) it is a henselian local ring; (vi) its residue field is algebraically closed; (vii) every $a \in A$ is congruent, modulo the maximal ideal of $A$, to some $c \in k₀$ with $c \in A$. (viii) There is a prime $\ell$ with $3 \le \ell$, $\ell \neq q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$, together with an element of $k₀$ that is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity. (ix) There is a unit $u$ of $A$ with $\pi_0^{q^2-1} = q\,u$. (x) There is a ring isomorphism $e : A₀ \simeq A \cap k₀$ compatible with $\iota$, in the sense that the image of $e(a)$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ equals $\iota(a)$ for all $a \in A₀$.
--
--   (xi) Bottom-layer clauses, for the trivial intermediate field $\bot$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ over $k₀$: an element of $\bot$ lies in the pullback of $A$ to $\bot$ if and only if its image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $A$; $\bot$ is finite-dimensional over $k₀$; the pullback of $A$ to $\bot$ is a discrete valuation ring and a henselian local ring; and there is a ring isomorphism $e_0$ from $A₀$ onto that pullback with the image of $e_0(a)$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ equal to $\iota(a)$ for all $a \in A₀$.
--
--   (xii) Finally, with `fieldBar q M'` regarded as a $k₀$-algebra through the composite of $k₀ \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$ and the constant embedding $\overline{\mathbb Q} \to$ `fieldBar q M'`, there is an intermediate field $F₀'$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $k₀$ such that: an element lies in $F₀'$ exactly when each of its Laurent coefficients is the image of some element of $k₀$; the compositum of $F₀'$ with the $k₀$-subfield generated by all constants from $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is all of `fieldBar q M'`; $F₀'$ is stable under `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` for every $\zeta'$ in `Idx q` and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; for every intermediate field $K'$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/k₀$ finite over $k₀$, every $m$, every family $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$ linearly independent over $K'$ and every family $a : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to$ `fieldBar q M'` with all $a_i$ in the compositum of $F₀'$ with the $k₀$-subfield generated by the constants from $K'$, the relation $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$ forces $a_i = 0$ for all $i$; every element of `fieldBar q M'` whose Laurent series lies in the range of `coeffEmb (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)`, i.e. has rational coefficients, belongs to $F₀'$; $F₀'$ and $F₀$ have exactly the same elements; and there is a ring isomorphism $\Phi$ from $F₀$ onto the compositum of $F₀'$ with the $k₀$-subfield generated by the constants coming from $\bot$, which is the identity on underlying elements of `fieldBar q M'`.
--
--   This is the bottom-layer case, for $q = 3$, of the descent of the geometric full-level function field at level $q^2M'$ to a small constant field: it produces an admissible constant field $k₀$ with the same elements as $K₀$ and tame element $\pi_0 = \pi$, together with the full package of valuation-theoretic properties of $A \cap k₀$, the trivial layer $\bot$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/k₀$, and an identification of the coefficient field $F₀$ with a $k₀$-rational level field inside `fieldBar q M'`. It is the input to the constructions of Igusa and Drinfeld charts and rings over the descended base, and is obtained by combining the admissibility statement [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_admissible_smallConstants_of_descentBase_of_eq_three`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_admissible_smallConstants_of_descentBase_of_eq_three) with the level-field statement [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_levelField_coeff_mem_sup_eq_top_levelAutBar_stable_linearDisjoint_of_eq_three`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_levelField_coeff_mem_sup_eq_top_levelAutBar_stable_linearDisjoint_of_eq_three).
